# Generated from: specs/238-present-issues-missing-spec-created-on-bare-write-spec/requirements.md
Feature: Bare write-spec missing-spec picker
  As an nmg-sdlc user
  I want bare write-spec to present open issues missing spec-created immediately
  So that I can choose the next specification without typing or reinvoking an issue number

  # --- Happy Path ---

  @SCN001
  Scenario: bare invocation immediately presents missing-spec issues
    Given a TUI invocation with empty arguments
    And open issues 9, 2, 7, and 4 lack exact label spec-created
    When write-spec starts
    Then the first interaction is one ask with issues 2, 4, and 7 in order
    And issue 2 is recommended
    And the last authored option is Finished — stop without writing a spec
    And no usage or enter-number gate precedes the ask

  @SCN002
  Scenario: a picker selection enters the existing first-spec path
    Given the bare picker is visible
    When the user selects a listed issue or enters a valid issue number through Other
    Then write-spec runs existing initial Discovery and Interview for that number
    And the first specification still finishes at xd://propose

  # --- Alternative Paths ---

  @SCN003
  Scenario Outline: non-empty arguments keep existing behavior
    Given write-spec starts with <arguments>
    When initial argument routing runs
    Then the bare picker is <picker>
    And the outcome is <outcome>

    Examples:
      | arguments | picker | outcome |
      | #42 | skipped | initial Discovery for 42 |
      | 42 | skipped | initial Discovery for 42 |
      | issue-42 | skipped | exact usage output |

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Finished stops silently
    Given the bare picker is visible
    When the user selects Finished — stop without writing a spec
    Then write-spec stops without Discovery
    And it prints no Published specs or Next step line

  # --- Error Handling ---

  @SCN005
  Scenario: listing failure fails closed
    Given the missing-spec-created helper cannot read valid issue and label evidence
    When bare write-spec starts
    Then it prints the helper failure reason
    And it does not ask or invent an issue list

  # --- Edge Cases ---

  @SCN006
  Scenario: no open issue is missing spec-created
    Given every open issue has exact label spec-created or there are no open issues
    When bare write-spec starts
    Then it prints exactly No open issues missing spec-created.
    And it stops without ask or usage

  @SCN007
  Scenario: post-publication continuation remains distinct
    Given a specification has been published
    When the continue loop runs
    Then it still uses approved-package candidates
    And its authored stop option remains Finished — stop writing specs
